.TH SAPHIRA-ROUTER 1 "2026" "saphira-router" "Saphira Linux"
.SH NAME
saphira-router \- Saphira Linux multi-tenant control plane
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira-router
.I init
.B \-\-user
.I NAME
.B \-\-password
.I SECRET
.br
.B saphira-router daemon
.br
.B saphira-router tui
.br
.B saphira-router
.I login
.B \-\-user
.I NAME
.br
.B saphira-router host list|enroll|caps
.br
.B saphira-router module list
.br
.B saphira-router capability
.I CODE
.SH DESCRIPTION
The control plane for load balancing, routing, virtual networking and
managed nodes.  One binary carries three roles: the daemon, the CLI and the
terminal interface.
.PP
The daemon is the
.B only writer
of persistent state.  The CLI and the TUI are clients of its local Unix
socket and never open the database themselves.  That is not a style rule: if a
client could write the database, authorization, the audit trail, the
transaction engine and the desired/observed separation would all be
bypassable by anyone who could reach the file.
.SH ROLES
.TP
.B init
Create the database, run migrations, and bootstrap the first tenant, user and
role.  The bootstrap administrator is a role with an enumerated set of
capabilities, not a wildcard: a capability introduced later does not join it
automatically.
.TP
.B daemon
Run the control plane.  Loads modules from the module directory, refuses an
incompatible ABI with a diagnostic, and serves the local API.  Run
unprivileged; it needs no privileged socket and no hardware access.
.TP
.B tui
The primary human interface.  Its sections are derived at runtime from the
module registry, so installing a module makes its functionality appear and
removing it makes it disappear, with no change to the interface.
.TP
.B anything else
The CLI, a thin client of the same API.  Every read and write command
supports
.BR \-\-json .
Exit codes distinguish denied, failed and partial so automation can tell them
apart.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SR_DB
Path to the SQLite database. Default
.IR /var/lib/saphira-router/router.db .
.TP
.B SR_SOCK
Path to the local control socket. Default
.IR /run/saphira-router/api.sock .
.TP
.B SR_SOCK_GROUP
Group permitted to reach the control socket, default
.BR wheel .
Membership is the only thing an operator needs to drive the control plane;
it confers NO database access.  The state directory stays 0750 to the
.B saphira-router
identity regardless.
.TP
.B SR_SOCK_MODE
Mode for the control socket, default 0660.
.TP
.B SR_MODULES
Module directory, scanned at startup. Default
.IR /usr/lib/saphira-router/modules .
The core is usable with this empty and with every module absent.
.TP
.B SR_TOKEN
A session token, so a script or the TUI can skip the login prompt.
.TP
.B HOME
A session token is cached in
.IR $HOME/.saphira-router/token ,
mode 0600.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/saphira-router/router.db
Core state. Writable only by the
.B saphira-router
identity.
.TP
.I /run/saphira-router/api.sock
The local control surface. Owner
.BR saphira-router ,
group as configured, mode 0660.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/saphira-router/modules
Module directory, discovered at runtime.
.TP
.I /etc/conf.d/saphira-router
Instance configuration read by both inits.
.SH SEE ALSO
The design documents shipped in
.IR /usr/share/doc/saphira-router/ .
